===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=sharp sound}}
{{onom|en|title=Imitative}} of the "click" sound; first recorded in the 1500s. Compare {{cog|stq|klikke||to click}}, {{cog|dum|clicken}} (Modern Dutch: {{m|nl|klikken||to click}}), Old High German {{m|goh|klecchen}} (Modern German: {{m|de|klecken}}, {{m|de|klicken||to click}}), Danish {{m|da|klikke||to click}}, Swedish {{m|sv|klicka||to click}}, Norwegian {{m|no|klikke||to click}}, Norwegian {{m|no|klekke||to hatch}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A brief, sharp, not particularly loud, relatively [[high-pitched]] sound produced by the impact of something small and hard against something hard, such as by the operation of a [[switch]], a [[lock]]{{,}} or a [[latch]].
#: {{ux|en|As I turned the key, the lock gave a '''click''' and the door opened.}}
#* {{RQ:Woolf Jacob's Room|chapter=1|passage=There was a '''click''' in the front sitting-room. Mr. Pearce had extinguished the lamp.}}
# {{lb|en|British}} The act of [[snap one's fingers|snapping one's fingers]].
# {{lb|en|phonetics}} An [[ingressive]] sound made by [[coarticulate|coarticulating]] a [[velar]] or [[uvular]] [[closure]] with another closure.
#: {{syn|en|click consonant}}
#: {{ux|en|[[tsk]] is a '''click''' in English.}}
# The sound made by a [[dolphin]].
# The act of operating a switch, etc., so that it [[#Verb|click]]s.
# {{lb|en|GUI}} The act of pressing a button on a computer [[mouse]] or similar input device, both as a physical act and a reaction in the software.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A single instance of content on the [[Internet]] being accessed.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-21|author=w:Oliver Burkeman|volume=189|issue=2|page=48|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly|url=http://www.theguardian.com/technology/2013/may/10/conscious-computing-twitter-facebook-google|title=The tao of tech|passage=The dirty secret of the internet is that all this distraction and interruption is immensely profitable. Web companies like to boast about{{...}}and so on. But the real way to build a successful online business is to be better than your rivals at undermining people's control of their own attention. Partly, this is a result of how online advertising has traditionally worked: advertisers pay for '''clicks''', and a '''click''' is a '''click''', however it's obtained.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261016230022/https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2013/may/10/conscious-computing-twitter-facebook-google|archivedate=16 October 2026}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Charles Arthur|title=Porn sites get more internet traffic in UK than social networks or shopping|date=2013-07-26|url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2013/jul/26/porn-sites-internet-traffic-uk|passage=Internet traffic to legal pornography sites in the UK comprised 8.5% of all "'''clicks'''" on web pages in June – exceeding those for shopping, news, business or social networks, according to new data obtained exclusively by the Guardian.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261016230022/https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2013/jul/26/porn-sites-internet-traffic-uk|archivedate=16 October 2026}}
# A [[pawl]] or similar [[catch]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1943|journal=Chilton's Jewelers' Circular
|passage=A wheel, with teeth in which a '''click''' or pawl engages to prevent backward motion; or the same with addition of another '''click''' through which power is imparted at intervals to move the wheel.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|slang|obsolete}} A [[knock]] or [[blow]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1808|author=Richard Graves|title=The Spiritual Quixote|page=127
|passage=This roused the tinker's choler, already provoked at Tugwell's amorous freedom with his doxy, and he gave him a '''click''' in the mazard. Tugwell had not been used tamely to receive a kick or a cuff; he, therefore, gave the tinker a rejoinder, {{...}}}}
# A [[limb]] [[contortion]] at the [[joint]], part of [[vogue]] [[dancing]].
# {{lb|en|music|informal}} A [[click track]].
#* {{quote-song|en|title={{w|Giorgio by Moroder}}|year=2013|lyricist={{w|Giorgio Moroder}}|artist={{w|Daft Punk}}|album={{w|Random Access Memories}}|text=But I knew I needed a '''click''', so we put a '''click''' on the 24-track, which then was synced to the Moog Modular.}}

